Fixes parallel indexers (MAGE_INDEXER_THREADS_COUNT > 1) failing with random, unrelated SQL errors,
e.g. during the catalog_category_product full reindex after a product import:
"Child process failed with message: SQLSTATE[42S22]: Column not found: 1054 Unknown column
'category_ids' in 'field list', query was: INSERT INTO `catalog_category_product_index_store12_tmp`
(`category_ids`, `country_of_manufacture`, ...) SELECT 398 AS `category_id`, `cp`.`entity_id` AS ..."

Root cause 1: Magento 2.4.9 builds every cache frontend on Symfony cache. SymfonyAdapterProvider is a
shared singleton that pools Redis connections per host:port:database. ProcessManager closes the DB and
AMQP connections before pcntl_fork(), but not the cache connections. The Symfony frontend adapter
detects the PID change and calls its cache factory again, yet the factory asks the same provider,
which hands back the parent's pooled connection. Every forked child therefore talks to Redis over the
one socket inherited from the parent, the request/response stream interleaves, and a process reads
another process's reply. In the error above, describeTable() of the tmp table was answered with an
unrelated cached array keyed by product attribute codes, so Full::reindexCategoriesBySelect() used
those keys as the INSERT column list.
Fix: the provider remembers the PID that owns its pool and drops the pooled connections when a
different PID asks for an adapter, so each child opens its own connection. The inherited handles are
only dereferenced, never closed, so the parent's socket is left intact.

Root cause 2: connections are persistent by default. phpredis keys persistent sockets by
host:port:persistent_id, so a child calling pconnect() with the parent's persistent_id would get the
inherited socket back even with a fresh pool.
Fix: the persistent_id is now "<persistent_id or 'default'>:<database>:<pid>". The database part keeps
frontends on different databases (default vs page_cache) from collapsing onto one persistent socket.

Root cause 3: the tag adapter is created once from the initial pool and kept its Redis connection
after the pool was rebuilt in a child.
Fix: Factory passes a tag adapter factory to the Symfony frontend adapter, which rebuilds the tag
adapter whenever it rebuilds the pool after a fork.

Covers plain 'redis' frontends and the remote level of 'symfony_l2' frontends, which is built through
the same Factory::createSymfonyCache() path.

Backport of upstream magento/magento2@19640e886e ("Solved indexer multi thread issue") plus the
persistent_id database scoping from magento/magento2@4d6f3a65a5 (both AC-17867 on 2.4-develop, not
part of the 2.4.9 tag). Drop this patch once the installed release contains these commits.

